# L0   { raw: 0, get value() { .. }, set value(next) { .. } }   one literal lays both halves, and the object is only read and stored into: both halves are proven, and `raw` beside them is filled
# L1   { get value() { .. } }  and  { }                         another allocation leaves the name out: nothing is proven
# L2   { get value() { .. } }  and  { set value(next) { .. } }  every object has an accessor there, and neither half is in every object
# L3   o = { }; o.value; lay the getter                         the body that makes the object reads the name in front of the definition
# L4   { get value() { .. } }; delete o.value                   an object loses the property
# RUN: link fields accesses layouts mechanisms=all
# CHECK: field L0.0 "raw" {{*}} filled
# CHECK: field L0.1 "value" {{*}}filled-by-accessors-alone accessor-from-birth
# CHECK-NOT: field L1.0 "value" {{*}}accessor-from-birth
# CHECK: field L2.0 "value" {{*}}accessor-from-birth
# CHECK-NOT: field L3.0 "value" {{*}}accessor-from-birth
# CHECK-NOT: field L4.0 "value" {{*}}accessor-from-birth
# CHECK: accessors L0.1 "value" getter=f2 proven setter=f3 proven
# CHECK-NOT: accessors L1.0 {{*}}proven
# CHECK-NOT: accessors L2.0 {{*}}proven
# CHECK-NOT: accessors L3.0 {{*}}proven
# CHECK-NOT: accessors L4.0 {{*}}proven
# CHECK: layout L0 {{*}}redefined-by-literals-alone

